      "formula": "Bedakan dengan tegas antara **Conjunction (diikuti Klausa: S + V)** dan **Preposition (diikuti Noun Phrase / V-ing)**:\n- **Conjunction (+ S + V):** `although, even though, though, because, since, as, while, whereas, when, if, unless, until, before, after`.\n- **Preposition (+ Noun Phrase / Gerund):** `despite, in spite of, because of, due to, owing to, during, unlike`.\n- **Coordinate Connectors (FANBOYS):** `for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so` menghubungkan dua klausa setara (`, but S + V`).\n- **Conjunctive Adverbs (`however, therefore, moreover, nevertheless`):** BUKAN penghubung koma! Harus diawali titik (`. However,`) atau titik koma (`; however,`).\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** Meletakkan `despite` sebelum `S + V` (salah!) atau meletakkan `although` / `because` sebelum Noun Phrase tanpa verb (salah!), serta kesalahan *double connector* (`Although..., but...` -- HARAM di TOEFL!).\n\n**WRONG:** **Despite** the server latency **was** extremely high, the cloud migration finished on schedule.\n**RIGHT:** **Although** the server latency **was** extremely high, the cloud migration finished on schedule. (OR: **Despite the extremely high server latency**, the cloud migration...)\n\n**WRONG:** **Although** quantum encryption is still expensive, **but** major banks are already testing it.\n**RIGHT:** **Although** quantum encryption is still expensive, major banks are already testing it. (Never combine \"although\" + \"but\"!)\n\n**Flashcard Q:** What is the structural difference between \"Although / Because / While\" and \"Despite / Because of / During\"?\n**Flashcard A:** Although, Because, and While are clause connectors requiring Subject + Verb; Despite, Because of, and During are prepositions requiring only a Noun Phrase or Gerund.\n\n---",
