      "formula": "- **Comparative (2 hal):** `-er + than` (1 suku kata: *faster than*) atau `more/less + Adj/Adv + than` (>=2 suku kata: *more efficient than*). **TIDAK BOLEH Double Comparative** (`more faster`, `more better` -> SALAH!).\n- **Superlative (>=3 hal):** `the + -est` atau `the most/least + Adj` (*the highest altitude of all*).\n- **Double Comparative (Semakin... semakin...):** `The + comparative (+ S + V), the + comparative (+ S + V)` (*The higher the altitude, the lower the air pressure.*).\n- **Perbandingan Logis (*Illogical Comparison*):** Bandingkan benda yang sejenis! Gunakan `that of` (tunggal) atau `those of` (jamak): *The climate of Bandung is cooler than **that of** Jakarta* (BUKAN *than Jakarta*).\n- **Pasangan wajib:** `the same ... as`, `similar to`, `different from`, `as + Adj/Adv + as`.\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** (1) Memakai superlative untuk 2 benda (`the tallest of the two` -> salah, harus `the taller of the two`), (2) `more + -er`, (3) Lupa `the` di klausa kedua Double Comparative, atau (4) Membandingkan *population* dengan *city* tanpa `that of`.\n\n**WRONG:** The storage capacity of solid-state drives is significantly **more faster** than traditional magnetic disks.\n**RIGHT:** The storage capacity of solid-state drives is significantly **faster** than **that of** traditional magnetic disks.\n\n**WRONG:** The more densely populated a coastal region becomes, **greater** the strain on its freshwater aquifers.\n**RIGHT:** The more densely populated a coastal region becomes, **the greater** the strain on its freshwater aquifers.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** Why is \"The salary of an architect is higher than a teacher\" grammatically flawed in TOEFL, and how do you fix it?\n**Flashcard A:** It makes an illogical comparison between a \"salary\" and a \"person (teacher)\". Fix it with \"that of\": \"The salary of an architect is higher than THAT OF a teacher.\"\n\n---",
