      "title": "Verb Tenses & Time Markers",
      "freq": "HIGH FREQUENCY - Part A & B",
      "formula": "Cari **Time Marker (penanda waktu)** terlebih dahulu untuk mengunci tense:\n- **Simple Past (V2):** `yesterday, ago, in 1995, last decade, during the nineteenth century, previously` (waktu lampau yang sudah selesai tuntas).\n- **Present Perfect (has/have + V3):** `since + titik waktu (since 2010)`, `for + durasi (for five years)`, `so far, recently, already, yet, over the past decade`.\n- **Past Perfect (had + V3):** Kejadian **lebih dulu terjadi** sebelum kejadian lampau lainnya (`By 1980, ... had V3`; `By the time + S + V2, S + had + V3`; `After S + had V3, S + V2`).\n- **Future Perfect (will have + V3):** `By 2035, ... will have V3`; `By the time + S + V1, S + will have + V3`.\n- **Kebiasaan vs Terbiasa:** `used to + V1` (dulu biasa dilakukan, sekarang tidak) vs `be/get used to + V-ing / Noun` (terbiasa dengan).\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** Memakai `has/have + V3` bersama tahun lampau spesifik (`in 1969` -> harus Simple Past `landed`, bukan `has landed`!), atau memakai Simple Past dengan `since 2015` (harus `has/have + V3`).\n\n**WRONG:** In 1928, Alexander Fleming **has discovered** penicillin while examining bacterial cultures.\n**RIGHT:** In 1928, Alexander Fleming **discovered** penicillin while examining bacterial cultures.\n\n**WRONG:** Since the fiber-optic submarine cable was activated in 2021, regional bandwidth **increased** dramatically.\n**RIGHT:** Since the fiber-optic submarine cable was activated in 2021, regional bandwidth **has increased** dramatically.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** What is the exact tense rule for \"By the time + Simple Past (V2)\" vs \"By the time + Simple Present (V1)\"?\n**Flashcard A:** \"By the time + S + V2\" pairs with Past Perfect (\"S + had + V3\"); \"By the time + S + V1\" pairs with Future Perfect (\"S + will have + V3\").\n\n---",
