      "freq": "HIGH FREQUENCY - Part A & B",
      "formula": "- **Passive Voice:** `be (is/am/are/was/were/been/be) + V3` (sering diikuti `by + agent` atau tanpa object langsung setelah verb transitif).\n- **Intransitive Verbs (TIDAK PERNAH BISA PASIF!):** `happen, occur, exist, appear, disappear, emerge, arise, rise, consist (of), belong (to), die, sleep, arrive, fall, remain, seem`. Jangan pernah menulis `was happened` atau `is consisted of`!\n- **Causative Verbs (Menyuruh/Meminta/Membuat):**\n  - **Active Causative (diikuti ORANG):** `have / make / let + Person + BARE V1` (*The professor had the assistant **check** the figures.*) vs `get + Person + TO V1` (*She got the technician **to repair** the router.*).\n  - **Passive Causative (diikuti BENDA):** `have / get + Thing + V3` (*We had the manuscript **edited** before submission.*).\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** Membuat kata kerja intransitif jadi pasif (`The earthquake was occurred in 2004`), lupa `to` setelah `get + person`, atau menambahkan `to` setelah `make + person` (`made him to rewrite` -> SALAH!).\n\n**WRONG:** The volcanic eruption **was occurred** shortly after seismic instruments recorded harmonic tremors.\n**RIGHT:** The volcanic eruption **occurred** shortly after seismic instruments recorded harmonic tremors.\n\n**WRONG:** Before publishing the findings, the laboratory director had the statistical tables **verify** by an external auditor.\n**RIGHT:** Before publishing the findings, the laboratory director had the statistical tables **verified** by an external auditor.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** Why is \"The sudden power outage was happened during the peak hour\" wrong, and what is the Causative Passive formula?\n**Flashcard A:** \"Happen\" is an intransitive verb and can NEVER be passive (correct: \"happened\"). Causative Passive formula: \"have / get + Object (Thing) + V3\" (e.g., \"had the car repaired\").\n\n---",
