      "title": "Word Form Mastery (Noun / Verb / Adjective / Adverb)",
      "freq": "HIGHEST FREQUENCY - Part B",
      "formula": "Ini adalah **soal PALING SERING muncul di Written Expression (No. 16-40)**! Kenali fungsi posisi kata (*syntactic slot*) dan akhiran (*suffix*) berikut:\n\n| Part of Speech | Syntactic Position (Where It Goes) | Classic TOEFL Suffixes | Example Family |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Noun (N)** | After articles (`a/an/the`), possessives (`its/their`), prepositions (`of/in/for`), adjectives | `-tion, -sion, -ment, -ity, -ance, -ence, -ness, -ship, -ism, -ist, -er/-or, -cy` | `creation, stability, significance, analyst` |\n| **Verb (V)** | After Subject, after modals (`can/will/must`), after `to` | `-ize, -ify, -ate, -en` | `create, stabilize, signify, analyze` |\n| **Adjective (Adj)** | Before Noun (`Adv + Adj + N`); after **Linking Verbs** (`be, seem, become, appear, remain, feel, look, sound, prove`) | `-al, -ive, -ous, -ic, -able, -ible, -ful, -less, -ant, -ent, -ary` | `creative, stable, significant, analytical` |\n| **Adverb (Adv)** | Modifies Verb (`work efficiently`), Adjective (`highly accurate`), Adverb (`very rapidly`), or Whole Sentence | `-ly` (EXCEPTIONS: `fast, hard, late, early, well`; beware Adj ending in `-ly`: `friendly, costly, likely, timely, lively`) | `creatively, stably, significantly, analytically` |\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** (1) Memakai Adjective untuk memodifikasi Verb atau Adjective lain (`extreme cold` -> harus `extremely cold`), (2) Memakai Adverb setelah Linking Verb (`remained calmly` -> harus `remained calm`), atau (3) Menaruh Verb/Adj setelah `the ... of` yang seharusnya Noun (`the stable of the bridge` -> harus `the stability of the bridge`).\n\n**WRONG:** Because the chemical reaction proceeds **rapid**, technicians must monitor the pressure valve **constant**.\n**RIGHT:** Because the chemical reaction proceeds **rapidly**, technicians must monitor the pressure valve **constantly**.\n\n**WRONG:** Despite intense economic volatility, the telecommunications sector remained **remarkably profitably**.\n**RIGHT:** Despite intense economic volatility, the telecommunications sector remained **remarkably profitable**. (Linking verb `remained` + Adv `remarkably` + Adj `profitable`!)\n\n**Flashcard Q:** Why is \"The solution appeared accurately\" wrong, while \"The sensor measured the voltage accurately\" is right?\n**Flashcard A:** \"Appear\" is a linking verb describing the subject, so it takes an ADJECTIVE (\"accurate\"). \"Measure\" is an action verb, so it is modified by an ADVERB (\"accurately\").\n\n---",
