      "title": "Countable vs Uncountable Quantifiers & Another/Other",
      "freq": "HIGH FREQUENCY - Part B",
      "formula": "- **Countable Plural Nouns:** `many, few, a few, fewer, several, a (large) number of`.\n- **Uncountable Nouns (SELALU TUNGGAL, tanpa `-s`, tanpa `a/an`):** `much, little, a little, less, a (great) deal of, an amount of`.\n- **Uncountable Traps WAJIB HAFAL di TOEFL:** `information, research, equipment, furniture, advice, news, evidence, knowledge, machinery, luggage, baggage, traffic, weather, progress, homework, software, hardware, money, work, music`. (TIDAK PERNAH `informations`, `equipments`, `researches`, `advices`!)\n- **Another vs Other vs Others:**\n  - `another + Singular Countable Noun` (*another experiment*)\n  - `other + Plural Noun / Uncountable Noun` (*other experiments*, *other information*)\n  - `the other + Singular/Plural Noun` (yang terakhir/sisa spesifik)\n  - `others` = pronoun berdiri sendiri (TIDAK diikuti noun!).\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** Memakai `amount of` untuk benda bisa dihitung (`a large amount of students` -> harus `number of`), memakai `much` untuk plural (`much factors` -> `many factors`), atau menulis `another factors` / `others factors`.\n\n**WRONG:** The new telemetry lab purchased **many advanced equipments** to gather **a large number of information**.\n**RIGHT:** The new telemetry lab purchased **much advanced equipment** (OR **many pieces of advanced equipment**) to gather **a large amount of information**.\n\n**WRONG:** Some renewable technologies rely on wind currents, while **others systems** capture tidal motion.\n**RIGHT:** Some renewable technologies rely on wind currents, while **other systems** (OR **others**) capture tidal motion.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** List 6 common uncountable nouns in TOEFL that NEVER take a plural \"-s\", and state when to use \"number of\" vs \"amount of\".\n**Flashcard A:** Information, equipment, research, furniture, advice, evidence (also news, knowledge, machinery). Use \"number of\" for countable plural nouns and \"amount of\" for uncountable nouns.\n\n---",
