      "title": "Articles (a / an / the / Zero Article) & Singular/Plural Agreement",
      "freq": "HIGH FREQUENCY - Part B",
      "formula": "- **`a` vs `an` bergantung BUNYI (Sound), BUKAN huruf:** `a university` (/ju:/), `a European country`, `a one-way street`, `a useful tool` vs `an hour` (silent h), `an honest error`, `an MBA degree` (/em/), `an X-ray`.\n- **Aturan Benda Tunggal Telanjang (*No Naked Singular*):** Singular Countable Noun TIDAK BOLEH berdiri sendiri tanpa determiner (`a/an/the/this/my/each`). Salah: *Engineer designed bridge.* Benar: ***An** engineer designed **the** bridge* atau ***Engineers** designed **bridges***.\n- **Gunakan `the`:** Superlative (`the most`), Ordinal (`the first/second`), Benda unik (`the Sun, the equator`), Sungai/Laut/Samudra/Pegunungan (`the Pacific Ocean, the Amazon, the Alps`), Negara jamak/berkata *Republic/United/Kingdom* (`the United States, the Netherlands, the Philippines`).\n- **Zero Article (tanpa `the`):** Bahasa (*English*), mata kuliah (*physics*), olahraga (*tennis*), benua (*Asia*), gunung tunggal (*Mount Merapi*), danau tunggal (*Lake Toba*), plural/uncountable general (*Computers have transformed society*).\n- **Irregular Academic Plurals (SANGAT SERING KELUAR!):** `criterion -> criteria`, `phenomenon -> phenomena`, `datum -> data`, `medium -> media`, `bacterium -> bacteria`, `analysis -> analyses`, `hypothesis -> hypotheses`, `crisis -> crises`, `thesis -> theses`, `fungus -> fungi`, `alumnus -> alumni`.\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** `a hour`, `an unique opportunity`, menulis `one of the criteria` tapi tidak sadar `criterion` itu tunggal dan `criteria` jamak (`this criteria` -> SALAH! Harus `this criterion` atau `these criteria`), atau membiarkan singular countable noun tanpa artikel.\n\n**WRONG:** Atmospheric refraction is **an unique optical phenomena** observed near the horizon at sunset.\n**RIGHT:** Atmospheric refraction is **a unique optical phenomenon** observed near the horizon at sunset.\n\n**WRONG:** **Most of scientists** agree that **the mathematics** is essential for machine learning.\n**RIGHT:** **Most scientists** agree that **mathematics** is essential for machine learning.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** Why is \"an European university\" wrong, and what are the singular vs plural forms of \"criteria\" and \"phenomena\"?\n**Flashcard A:** \"European\" begins with a consonant /y/ sound, so it requires \"a European university\". Singular: criterion / phenomenon; Plural: criteria / phenomena.\n\n---",
