      "title": "Gerunds (V-ing) vs Infinitives (to V1)",
      "freq": "HIGH FREQUENCY - Part A & B",
      "formula": "Kata kerja tertentu hanya boleh diikuti **Gerund (`V-ing`)**, sementara kata kerja lain wajib diikuti **Infinitive (`to + V1`)**:\n\n| Category | High-Frequency TOEFL / EPrT Verb & Expression List | Pattern |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **ALWAYS + Gerund (`V-ing`)** | `admit, appreciate, avoid, consider, delay, deny, discuss, enjoy, finish, keep, mind, miss, postpone, practice, quit, recommend, resist, risk, suggest, tolerate` | `Verb + V-ing` (*avoid making*) |\n| **ALWAYS + Infinitive (`to V1`)** | `afford, agree, appear, arrange, attempt, claim, decide, demand, deserve, expect, fail, hesitate, hope, intend, learn, manage, offer, plan, prepare, pretend, promise, refuse, seem, tend, threaten, want` | `Verb + to V1` (*manage to solve*) |\n| **Preposition `to` + `V-ing` TRAP!** | `look forward to, be accustomed to, be used to, object to, be committed to, be dedicated to, contribute to, in addition to, lead to, be opposed to` | `... to + V-ing` (*look forward to meeting*) |\n| **All Other Prepositions + `V-ing`** | `in, on, at, by, for, of, from, with, without, about, before, after, instead of, capable of, succeed in, prevent from` | `Prep + V-ing` (*by reducing*) |\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** Melihat kata `to` lalu refleks memilih `V1`, padahal `to` di `look forward to`, `be used to`, `object to`, `dedicated to`, dan `contribute to` adalah **preposisi**, sehingga WAJIB diikuti `V-ing`!\n\n**WRONG:** The municipal council is committed to **expand** bike lanes and expects **reducing** downtown congestion.\n**RIGHT:** The municipal council is committed to **expanding** bike lanes and expects **to reduce** downtown congestion.\n\n**WRONG:** Because of severe budget cuts, the observatory could not afford **upgrading** its primary mirror.\n**RIGHT:** Because of severe budget cuts, the observatory could not afford **to upgrade** its primary mirror.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** Why does \"contribute to\" and \"be accustomed to\" take V-ing instead of V1?\n**Flashcard A:** In these expressions, \"to\" is a PREPOSITION (not an infinitive marker), and prepositions are always followed by a noun or gerund (V-ing), e.g., \"contribute to reducing emissions.\"\n\n---",
