      "title": "Redundancy, Word Order & The 10-Second Written Expression Scan Checklist",
      "freq": "HIGHEST ROI - Part B",
      "formula": "1. **Redundancy Traps (Pemborosan Kata):** Hindari kata bermakna ganda: `repeat again` (cukup `repeat`), `return back` (`return`), `advance forward` (`advance`), `sufficient enough` (`sufficient` atau `enough`), `annual yearly` (`annual`), `new innovation` (`innovation`), `same identical` (`identical`), `the reason is because` (WAJIB `the reason is that`!).\n2. **Noun Adjunct Singular Rule:** Kata benda yang berfungsi sebagai kata sifat di depan benda lain **SELALU TUNGGAL** (`a five-year contract`, BUKAN `five-years`; `a two-hundred-page manual`, BUKAN `pages`; `shoe store`, BUKAN `shoes store`).\n3. **Word Order Traps:**\n   - `Adj + enough` (*fast enough*) vs `enough + Noun` (*enough bandwidth*).\n   - `Modifier + Noun`: `a remarkably efficient engine` (Adv -> Adj -> Noun).\n   - `both/all` sebelum `the/these/my`: `all the participants` (BUKAN `the all participants`).\n\n**Classic EPrT Trap:** Mengira `a ten-stories building` benar karena ada angka 10, atau menulis `the reason why he resigned was because...`.\n\n**WRONG:** The civil engineering department completed a **twelve-months** feasibility study to **return back** to the original site.\n**RIGHT:** The civil engineering department completed a **twelve-month** feasibility study to **return** to the original site.\n\n**WRONG:** The main reason for the satellite's signal loss was **because** solar radiation damaged its transponder.\n**RIGHT:** The main reason for the satellite's signal loss was **that** solar radiation damaged its transponder.\n\n**Flashcard Q:** Why is \"a three-hours exam\" wrong, and what must replace \"The reason is because...\" in formal EPrT English?\n**Flashcard A:** A noun modifier before another noun (\"three-hour\") must ALWAYS be singular (\"a three-hour exam\"). \"The reason is because\" is redundant; always use \"The reason is THAT...\".\n\n> **STRATEGY: The 10-Second Written Expression Scan Algorithm (Questions 16-40)**\n> Saat menghadapi soal Error Identification (No. 16-40), JANGAN membaca seperti novel. Jalankan 6 langkah scan ini berurutan pada keempat bagian bergaris bawah (A, B, C, D):\n> 1. **VERB CHECK (2 sec):** Cek apakah verb cocok dengan Head Subject (abaikan prepositional phrase!), cek tense vs time marker, cek active vs passive.\n> 2. **WORD FORM CHECK (2 sec):** Cek akhiran setiap kata bergaris bawah (`-tion` vs `-al` vs `-ly`). Apakah posisinya butuh Noun, Verb, Adj, atau Adv?\n> 3. **PARALLELISM CHECK (2 sec):** Ada `and / or / but / than / both...and / not only...but also`? Pastikan bentuk kiri dan kanan identik!\n> 4. **CONNECTOR / CLAUSE CHECK (2 sec):** Cek `although/despite`, `because/because of`, `which/where/that`, double verb, atau dangling modifier.\n> 5. **NOUN / ARTICLE / PRONOUN CHECK (1 sec):** Cek singular/plural (`another/other`, `number/amount`, uncountable `-s`, `criteria/phenomena`, `its/their`, `five-year`).\n> 6. **COLLOCATION / CONFUSED WORD CHECK (1 sec):** Cek preposisi tetap (`superior to`, `capable of`, `consist of`) dan pasangan jebakan (`make/do`, `like/alike`, `rise/raise`, `almost/most`, `percent/percentage`).\n\n---",
